    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nObserve the following screen recording where I start neovim with `VIMINIT=\"lua vim.opt.background = 'light'\" build/bin/nvim`. Note that the background starts out \"light\", and after backgrounding and foregrounding neovim, it becomes \"dark\":\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b35296e4-89bd-4f9e-b719-a932fd8d5c1c\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Run this in a terminal that supports OSC 11 (I'm using alacritty):\n   ```console\n   $ VIMINIT=\"lua vim.opt.background = 'light'\" build/bin/nvim\n   ```\n2. `:set background?` should return `background=light`.\n3. Then send neovim to the background with `ctrl-z`, and bring it back to the foreground with `fg`.\n4. `:set background?` now erroneously returns `background=dark`.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nI expect my explicitly configured background to not change. That's clearly the intent of this code, it refuses to update the background if `bg_user_set` returns `true`: https://github.com/neovim/neovim/blob/6a6431cb99f411a85ffb3157023cd4726614485d/runtime/lua/vim/_core/defaults.lua#L962-L965\n\nI spent entirely too long debugging this, and I believe the root cause is that:\n\n1. `main.c` calls `nlua_init_defaults()`, which (indirectly) loads `runtime/lua/vim/_core/defaults.lua`: https://github.com/neovim/neovim/blob/6a6431cb99f411a85ffb3157023cd4726614485d/src/nvim/main.c#L459\n2. `detect_background` makes a osc11 request: https://github.com/neovim/neovim/blob/6a6431cb99f411a85ffb3157023cd4726614485d/runtime/lua/vim/_core/defaults.lua#L948\n3. We get a response to the osc11 request, but at this point `bg_user_set` returns `false` (note that we haven't loaded `VIMINIT` yet), so we keep the osc11 listener around.\n4. We call `source_startup_scripts` https://github.com/neovim/neovim/blob/6a6431cb99f411a85ffb3157023cd4726614485d/src/nvim/main.c#L481\n5. `source_startup_scripts` calls `do_user_initialization()`: https://github.com/neovim/neovim/blob/6a6431cb99f411a85ffb3157023cd4726614485d/src/nvim/main.c#L2227\n6. `do_user_initialization` invokes `VIMINIT` with `execute_env`: https://github.com/neovim/neovim/blob/6a6431cb99f411a85ffb3157023cd4726614485d/src/nvim/main.c#L2095\n7. `execute_env` sets `current_sctx.sc_sid = SID_ENV` (-4) before invoking the code in `VIMINIT`: https://github.com/neovim/neovim/blob/6a6431cb99f411a85ffb3157023cd4726614485d/src/nvim/main.c#L22523.\n8. `vim.opt.background = 'light'` in `VIMINIT` goes through [`api_set_sctx` which sets `current_sctx.sc_sid = SID_LUA;` (-8)](https://github.com/neovim/neovim/blob/0653e7a338e888d7b98143b8aa85865d843eefb7/src/nvim/api/private/helpers.c#L1061) (I'm handwaving a bit here, I haven't actually stepped through the code, but my printf debugging leads me to believe this is true) before setting the `background`. **This means that the `last_set_sid` for the background option is -8, which is going to cause problems later on, because that's [the sid that `bg_user_set` uses](https://github.com/neovim/neovim/blob/6a6431cb99f411a85ffb3157023cd4726614485d/runtime/lua/vim/_core/defaults.lua#L835-L837) to detect if `background` was set explicitly by the user.**\n9. Background neovim and then foreground neovim. This triggers this call to `tui_query_bg_color_noflush` to detect any color changes that occurred while neovim was backgrounded: https://github.com/neovim/neovim/blob/6a6431cb99f411a85ffb3157023cd4726614485d/src/nvim/tui/tui.c#L605-L608\n10. The osc11 listener registered in step 2) is still around. It fires, but `bg_user_set` **still returns `false`**, which means we go on to update `background`.\n\ntl;dr: the issue is that lua code setting `background` during `VIMINIT` stored a `last_set_sid` of -8, which causes [`bg_user_set`](https://github.com/neovim/neovim/blob/6a6431cb99f411a85ffb3157023cd4726614485d/runtime/lua/vim/_core/defaults.lua#L840C18-L840C29) to erroneously return `false`.\n\n\nThis is unfortunately of those situations where knowing the root cause does not lead me to any bright ideas about how to fix it :cry:.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nv0.13.0-dev-934+g6a6431cb99\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nno, 9.2.0389 (this is lua specific stuff)\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nNixOS 26.11 (Zokor)\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nAlacritty 0.17.0\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nalacritty\n\n### Installation\n\nbuild from repo",
