            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "> And what if you use `-c`/`--cmd` and set the background there?\n\nI see the same issue. If I run:\n\n```console\n$ build/bin/nvim --cmd \"lua vim.opt.background = 'light'; print('loaded --cmd. just set background to light, background.last_set_sid = ' .. vim.inspect(vim.api.nvim_get_option_info2('background', {}).last_set_sid));\"\n```\n\nI see this message (the `last_set_sid` being -8 is the problem):\n\n> loaded --cmd. just set background to light, background.last_set_sid = -8\n>\n> hmm, it should be `SID_ENV` for `VIMINIT`:\n\n@justinmk, did you see step 8 in my explanation above? I'll admit this is the part I dug into least, but printf debugging showed me that `current_sctx.sc_sid` is getting set to `SID_LUA` here: https://github.com/neovim/neovim/blob/0653e7a338e888d7b98143b8aa85865d843eefb7/src/nvim/api/private/helpers.c#L1061\n\nDoes that sound plausible?\n\n> The issue is that detect_background() calls reset() on the OptionSet before checking if the user already explicitly set 'background'.\n\n@cschanhniem, I don't see a call to `reset()` in [`detect_background`](https://github.com/neovim/neovim/blob/0653e7a338e888d7b98143b8aa85865d843eefb7/runtime/lua/vim/_core/defaults.lua#L932). Furthermore, you can verify with `vim.inspect(vim.api.nvim_get_option_info2('background', {}).last_set_sid)` that  the issue occurs at the point we set the background (in `VIMINIT`, or `--cmd`).",
